{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/83491-gmc-conversion-of-corebook-ghosts-stopgap-for-clarity-s-sake","id":83491,"title":"GMC Conversion of Corebook Ghosts (Stopgap, for clarity's sake)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-03T14:54:57-08:00","id":83491,"title":"GMC Conversion of Corebook Ghosts (Stopgap, for clarity's sake)","content":"Going mostly by Numina count and Attribute dot totals\u2026<br /> <br /> From WoD Core:<br /> <br /> Apparitions and Poltergeists are Rank 1 (the former being near the lower bound with 5 Attribute dots and 1 Numen, the latter being on the high end with 8 Attribute dots and 3 Numina).<br /> <br /> Deceivers and Skinriders are Rank 2 (the former being somewhere in the middle of the category's scope with 11 Attribute dots and 3 Numina, the latter being high up in the Rank with 14 Attribute dots and 5 Numina [though this may be complicated by one of those being Possession, which is noted as a rare ability for ghosts]).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T14:55:32-08:00","id":83492,"title":"","content":"From Geist Core:<br /> <br /> Ghost trees are Rank 2 (12 Attribute dots, 3 Numina, possibly unusual Manifestation effect represented by being a tree visible to everyone).<br /> <br /> The sample noncombatant ghosts, from their sentience and dicepools, seem to be Rank 2.<br /> <br /> Geister and Kerberoi are complicated by the inclusion of Keys, Manifestations, and/or Psyche scores (seeing as the system pre-dates Influence mechanics for ghosts and none of them have more than a full handful of Numina that are denoted as Numina and the River chart's near-equivalence to the Rank chart clashes with the provisional statement that both are modeled as higher-Ranking ghosts).<br /> <br /> For simplicity's sake, Kerberoi might be guessed to be of a Rank equal to their River count. The Horned Fiend, by Attribute count, is Rank 3, though Ithmah and Mother's Traits in the same categories would mark them as Rank 2 and the Fiend is called out as notably powerful; treating Psyche as effective Rank makes this somewhat simpler, but still leaves us with the perplexing outcome of Mother being Rank 2. The Clockwork Hive and the Triptych, matching the chart as they do, appear to be effectively Rank 2 and 5, respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T14:56:59-08:00","id":83495,"title":"","content":"Looking over at Book of the Dead for ideas\u2026<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Family Man has the Attribute dot and Numina count for a Rank 3 (and is Psyche 3).<br /> <br /> Whatever El Diablo is, he's got the Attributes for a Rank 3 (18 dots), but not the Numina count, and the lack of an Essence listing makes it difficult to guess more than that.<br /> <br /> Clockwork's got the Attributes of a Rank 3, as does Dominus, but both are 1-River Kerberoi with two Numina each; their Dominion's three Old Laws and noted shallowness suggest instead Rank 1 or 2.<br /> <br /> The Judges, with nine Numina (counting non standards like Unfettered and One Step Behind) and 24 Attribute dots, seem to just about fit into the Rank 3 box, and Yama, with 27 Attribute dots and seven Numina, could likewise be Rank 4. Lowgate Prison has four Old Laws, which ostensibly puts its Kerberos at Rank 3 at most.<br /> <br /> The Victor has 32 Attribute dots, 6 Numina, and four Old Laws - Rank 4 by the first one, Rank 3 by either of the other two.<br /> <br /> The Forge of Orcus has five Old Laws, suggesting Rank 3 at most, and Orcus's Attribute total (25) corroborates this. Erra has the Attributes of a Rank 3 entity (21 total) but only five Numina, and she and her sisters have no memory of the living world; one theory put forth is that they used to serve a deathlord &quot;until he fell into an eternal slumber of disuse.&quot;<br /> <br /> Oppia has five Old Laws as well, and its Kerberoi have a total of 18 Attribute dots, both of which suggest Rank 3. Plenty's origin suggests things can be found in the Rivers, his Attribute spread (28) suggests a Rank of 4, and he has three Numina (though no Psyche score is given).<br /> <br /> The Athenaeum has eight Old Laws, suggesting its Kerberos has a maximum Rank of 4, but Enoch only has 23 Attribute dots to his name, so it seems more likely that he is Rank 3.<br /> <br /> Mictlan's Old Laws are either eight or arbitrarily many, but Polydegmon's Attribute spread unambiguously indicates he's Rank 5.<br /> <br /> The Grave Dream has eight Old Laws, and the Dark Man has 21 Attribute dots; Rank 3 seems to be the indication.<br /> <br /> The Ocean of Fragments has twelve Old Laws (either four or five Rivers down, by the chart), but its Kerberos is only given stats for the purposes of attempting to deal with it temporarily (32 Attribute dots, which is the same total as the Admiral and about flush with a Rank 4 entity or a fragment of a stronger being).</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}